## SQ-GF31-03 | Sputter cannot be built (new row)
@group A
@commands bot places a carved pumpkin on a barrel; `execute if entity @e[type=nock_enough_arrows:sputter]`
@pass test fails, the pumpkin stays
@fails `config/nock_enough_arrows-common.toml` `enableSputter` not false on the server copy
@from batches/r1031/a1_world.qb
# self-contained since r1118 (judge-3, 2026-11-18): bot spawn from r1101 p1_server / r1031 a1_world, a2_variants bot row
> execute unless entity qa run pbot spawn qa 0 -60 0 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> setblock 45 -60 0 minecraft:barrel
> tp qa 45 -60 2
# a bot use on a barrel opens it (no sneak): setblock runs the same CarvedPumpkinBlock.onPlace pattern check
> setblock 45 -59 0 minecraft:carved_pumpkin
sleep 3
> execute if entity @e[type=nock_enough_arrows:sputter]
> execute if block 45 -59 0 minecraft:carved_pumpkin
expect Test failed
expect Test passed
reject (?i)unknown entity|invalid
look "Test failed" must come from the sputter check and "Test passed" from the pumpkin check

